# The clean API: LLM → Bot (commands) & Bot → LLM (events)

**Command envelope (LLM → Bot)**
Concrete, no wiggle words. Every command returns a status and a digest for memory.

```json
{
  "cmd_id": "d8b2f1",
  "commands": [
    {"type":"say", "text":"On my way! Show me the best catch."},
    {"type":"navigate_to", "target":{"plot_id":"corey-dock"}, "timeout_sec":45},
    {"type":"look_at", "target":{"tag":"fishing_sign"}},
    {"type":"interact", "target":{"tag":"start_button"}},
    {"type":"linger", "duration_sec":90, "goal":"evaluate_fun"}
  ],
  "policy": {
    "safety": {"avoid_lava":true, "stay_breathable":true},
    "abort_on": ["stuck", "walled_off", "player_disconnected"]
  }
}
```

**Event envelope (Bot → LLM)**
Bot publishes high-signal events. The LLM can reply with more commands or just update memory.

```json
{
  "event":"entered_plot",
  "ts": 1739695200,
  "ai_id":"ai-ada",
  "plot":{"id":"corey-dock","owner":"corey","tax_open":true},
  "context":{"players_nearby":["corey","tuttle"],"signs":["Welcome to FishDock v2"],"ambient":"ocean"}
}
```

Other event types: `chat_heard`, `object_detected`, `stuck`, `arrived`, `timer_expired`, `hazard_detected`, `wall_detected`, `points_accrual_tick`.

